Root cause:
The bug in `TestFSInputChecker` was likely caused by the improper handling of file length and input stream management in the `ChecksumFileSystem` class. The original implementation may not have correctly accounted for the file length when reading data, leading to failures in checksum verification during tests. The introduction of the `FSDataBoundedInputStream` class aims to address this by providing a more robust way to manage input streams and file length.

