```
```java
return new FSDataBoundedInputStream(fs, f, in);
```
Reason:
The introduction of the `FSDataBoundedInputStream` class provides a more robust way to manage input streams and file length. By using this new class, the system can ensure that the input stream is properly bounded by the actual file length, which helps prevent issues related to incorrect data reading and checksum verification. This change addresses the root cause of the bug by ensuring that the input stream management is handled correctly.


